# Commits whose diff is formatting only. `git blame` skips them and names the
# commit that wrote the code instead.
#
# This file does nothing on its own. Each clone has to opt in:
#
#   git config blame.ignoreRevsFile .git-blame-ignore-revs
#
# A sha that does not resolve is ignored SILENTLY — no warning, exit 0 — so a
# typo here reads exactly like a working entry. `test/blame-ignore-revs.test.ts`
# is what catches that.

# The one-time Prettier adoption: 320 files, 37,669 lines.
#
# It is the SQUASH, so it also carries ~240 lines of real change across 16
# files. Blame on those lines names the commit before it, which is wrong. The
# pure reformat (fb15837) was squashed away and is unreachable, so there is no
# formatting-only sha to name instead.
